# Phase 3
# Captured 2026-07-28 on Jetson Orin Nano Dev Kit (JetPack 6 / L4T R36.4.7,
# qemu-system-aarch64 6.2.0, host kernel 5.15.148-tegra). Guest-side serial
# log for the Phase-3 QNX<->Linux TCP IPC benchmark (docs/orin-port.md).
#
# ifs.bin + disk-qemu were REBUILT from the qnx-safety-vm/ Phase-1 baseline
# (mkqnximage --type=qemu --arch=aarch64le --hostname=qnx-safety --build) to
# stage the new ipc-test/qnx-server-net/qnx-echo-server-net binary into the
# IFS and auto-start it (see qnx-safety-vm/local/snippets/{ifs_files,post_start}.custom).
# post_start.custom also forces vtnet0's static IP (192.168.100.10/24) since
# OPT_IP=dhcp never gets a lease on br0 (no DHCP server there, see
# scripts/orin/setup-bridge-orin.sh).
#
# Command (scripts/orin/launch-qnx-on-orin-tcg.sh):
#   sudo qemu-system-aarch64 -machine virt,gic-version=3 -accel tcg -cpu max \
#     -smp 2 -m 1G -drive file=disk-qemu,if=none,id=drv0,format=raw \
#     -device virtio-blk-device,drive=drv0 \
#     -netdev tap,id=n0,ifname=tap-qnx,script=no,downscript=no \
#     -device virtio-net-device,netdev=n0,mac=52:54:00:11:11:11 \
#     -object rng-random,filename=/dev/urandom,id=rng0 \
#     -device virtio-rng-device,rng=rng0 \
#     -kernel ifs.bin -nographic -serial file:boot-ipc.log \
#     -display none -no-reboot -monitor none
#
# Four real client connections are visible below, one per benchmark run
# during this same guest boot: a 70-frame smoke test (50 timed + 20
# warm-up), a 2000-frame 1000/1000 run, and two full 101000-frame
# (100000 timed + 1000 warm-up) runs. Frame counts match the Linux client's
# own accounting exactly (see orin-tcg-qnx-ipc-client1.log for the second
# 101000-frame run) -- 100000+ round trips with zero mismatch, zero stall,
# unlike the Phase-2 cloud leg's non-deterministic virtio-console stall at
# ~15 samples (ipc-test/qnx-host-client/README.md).

